Collections framework consists of interface that provides some common methods
to work with different objects.

Before Java version 2 i.e. jdk 1.2, different classes like ArrayList, LinkedList Vector, Stack
used to have different methods and it was a tedious tasks to remember all these.

So version 2 collections framework was introduced which provides a common set of interfaces
for all these classes.

Hierarchy of collections framework is as follows:
Iterable->Collection->List->ArrayList,LinkedList,Vector,Stack,CopyOnWriteArrayList
                    ->Set->HashSet,LinkedHashSet,TreeSet,EnumSet,SortedSet,CopyOnWriteArraySet
                    ->Queue->LinkedList,PriorityQueue,Deque->ArrayDeque,LinkedList,ConcurrentLinkedDeque
Map->HashMap,LinkedHashMap
